add(129,'Circle regions','In a circle of radius $r$, chord $AB$ subtends $0<\\theta<\\pi$ at the centre. A semicircle with diameter $AB$ is constructed outside the minor circular segment. Let $T$ be the triangle formed by the centre and $A,B$. Let $B_s$ be the semicircle area minus the minor-segment area.',[('Show that the minor-segment area is $\\frac12r^2(\\theta-\\sin\\theta)$.',2),('Show that the semicircle area is $\\frac\\pi4r^2(1-\\cos\\theta)$.',4),('Given that the area of $T$ equals twice $B_s$, find $\\theta$.',7)],[[A('Sector area is $\\frac12r^2\\theta$.'),A('Subtract triangle area $\\frac12r^2\\sin\\theta$.')],[M('Bisect the central triangle.'),A('$AB=2r\\sin(\\theta/2)$.'),A('Semicircle radius is $r\\sin(\\theta/2)$, so area is $\\frac12\\pi r^2\\sin^2(\\theta/2)$.'),A('Use $\\sin^2(\\theta/2)=(1-\\cos\\theta)/2$ to get the stated expression.')],[A('$B_s=\\frac\\pi4r^2(1-\\cos\\theta)-\\frac12r^2(\\theta-\\sin\\theta)$.'),M('Set $\\frac12r^2\\sin\\theta=2B_s$.'),A('Cancel the positive factor $r^2$.'),A('$\\theta-\\frac12\\sin\\theta-\\frac\\pi2(1-\\cos\\theta)=0$.'),M('Solve numerically over $0<\\theta<\\pi$.'),A(f'Interior root $\\theta={root:.8f}$ radians.'),A(f'$\\theta={N(root)}$ radians; $0$ and $\\pi$ are excluded endpoints.')]],note='New region relation preserves the original circle/semicircle area method; interior root located by bracketing and substituted into the original area equation.')
