add(140,'Ferris wheel modelling','An observation wheel has diameter $100$ m, and its lowest point is $12$ m above the ground. It rotates at a constant rate of three complete revolutions per hour. A passenger starts at the lowest point at $t=0$, where $t$ is measured in minutes. Model the height by $h(t)=c+a\\cos(bt)$.',[('Find the maximum height and period.',4),('Find $a,b,c$.',5),('Find the passenger’s height after $7$ minutes.',2),('Find the total time above $72$ m during the first revolution.',5)],[[M('Add the diameter to the lowest height.'),A('Maximum $112$ m.'),M('Period $=60/3$ minutes.'),A('Period $20$ minutes.')],[A('$c=(112+12)/2=62$.'),A('Amplitude $50$.'),RR('The passenger starts at the minimum, hence $a=-50$.'),M('$b=2\\pi/T$.'),A('$b=\\pi/10$.')],[M('Substitute $t=7$ into $62-50\\cos(\\pi t/10)$.'),A(f'$h(7)={N(62-50*math.cos(.7*math.pi))}$ m.')],[M('$h>72$ is equivalent to $\\cos(\\pi t/10)<-1/5$.'),A(f'The first crossing is $t_1=(10/\\pi)\\arccos(-1/5)={tfirst:.8f}$ minutes.'),A('The second crossing is $20-t_1$ by symmetry.'),M('Subtract the crossing times: $20-2t_1$.'),A(f'Total time $={N(duration)}$ minutes.')]],note='Source Q140 has only introductory wheel data; reconstructed complete modelling sequence to its advertised 16 marks. Period, endpoints and threshold times verified numerically.')
